// The shipped quality tiers (spec §3.1, §5.12 "Quality tiers"), compiled into the renderer:
// `sapphire_render::quality::TierTable::shipped`, whose module docs say what reads each knob.
// Every number is a Proposal until M2 measures the reference devices at thermally throttled
// clocks (spec §3).
//
// - Drawn from today: `resolution`, `antialiasing`, `bloom_levels`, `light_path`, `max_lights`,
//   `sky`, `environment`, `shadows`, `post_effects`, `foliage`, `ambient_occlusion` and
//   `reflections`, plus `frame_rate` and `gpu_frame_ms` as dynamic resolution's targets.
// - `post_effects` (M1 P3): the radial blur's taps per pixel along its streak, in groups of four.
//   A pixel's taps start at a per-pixel offset, so fewer taps read as finer grain rather than as
//   copies of the frame; phones take 8 (spec §5.12's P3 note has the costs).
// - `sky` (M1 W2): the sky cube's size and frames between face updates, and the cirrus layer.
//   Both desktop tiers draw the same sky, so golden images match on every desktop GPU.
// - `environment` (M1 W4): the environment shader's specular model. Desktop tiers take the full
//   GGX (distribution, height-correlated Smith visibility, Schlick Fresnel); Mobile-High a
//   cheaper GGX that folds visibility and Fresnel into one term; Mobile-Low none, where the world
//   reads by its painted diffuse (terminator, wrap, shadow tint, band, desaturation and emission
//   run on every tier). Both desktop tiers draw the same, as with the sky. And where it reads a
//   probe grid (M1 W5, `probes`): per pixel, or per vertex on Mobile-Low, where the per-pixel
//   lookup cost 38% of its main pass at 1080p (spec §5.12 "Lighting" has the numbers).
// - `foliage` (M1 W6): how many of the wind's levels run (trunk sway, branch bend, leaf flutter),
//   alpha-to-coverage for alpha-tested cards under MSAA, and translucency through leaves. Desktop
//   tiers resolve cards with TAA (MSAA is off, so alpha-to-coverage never applies) and run every
//   level with translucency. Phones cover cards' edges in tile memory with alpha-to-coverage;
//   Mobile-Low keeps trunks and branches moving but drops the leaves' flutter, which a 590-row
//   scene barely resolves, and translucency, a per-pixel `pow` the canopy reads without.
// - `ambient_occlusion` (M1 W5): capsule AO from the characters' bodies on every tier, a short
//   loop per pixel; GTAO at half resolution on desktop (two slices of four steps out to 1 m, the
//   same on both desktop tiers, as with the sky) and Mobile-High (one slice of four steps, out to
//   0.75 m), none on Mobile-Low, whose budget row has no figure (spec §3.3).
// - `reflections` (M1 W5): the sky cube prefiltered into roughness mips for a probe grid's
//   environment specular, half the sky cube's size; Mobile-Low has no environment specular, so
//   none is made there.
// - Read by later packages: `volumetric_fog`, `screen_space_outlines` (C4), `max_particles`
//   (sapphire_vfx, M2) and `lod_bias` (LOD selection).
//
// Shadows (M1 R4, look pillar 4; `sapphire_render::shadows`): spec §3.3 budgets 2 ms for 4
// cascades on desktop and 3 ms for 2 on phones. The far half of the cascades is cached, drawn in
// turns (the far two alternate on desktop; the far one every other frame on phones), which spends
// the budget where the camera is. Desktop characters near the camera draw maps of their own for
// crisp contact shadows (8 at most, `character_resolution` each); phones cast every character's
// capsule instead, which costs no pass. The filter is a 5 × 5 tent on desktop and 3 × 3 on
// phones, whose lower cascade resolution already softens it. Distances end where the anime look
// still reads a shadow's shape at each tier's resolution; past them a baked far term will take
// over (shadows module docs, "Later milestones").
//
// Antialiasing (M1 R7, look pillar 6): desktop tiers resolve with temporal AA and MSAA off.
// TAA's jittered history resolves edges inside a surface (painted shadow-bias steps, the
// unfiltered material-ID borders of control maps, thin highlights) as well as silhouettes and
// outlines, where MSAA resolves only geometry, and the scene prepass it reads holds
// single-sampled depth and velocity. 4× MSAA on top would quadruple the main pass's attachments
// for edges TAA already resolves. Phones keep 4× MSAA in tile memory instead (transient
// attachments, cleared and discarded on tile): no history and nothing to smear, and no prepasses
// but the scene prepass GTAO reads on Mobile-High (M1 W5).
//
// Resolution: TAA also upsamples, so the desktop tiers keep spec §3.1's internal heights:
// Desktop-High renders at most 1440 rows (1440p native, 4K from 1440), Desktop-Low 1080. Below
// those heights they render at native height. The mobile tiers' caps upsample in post's final
// pass, bilinearly, until a spatial upscaler arrives.
(
    type: "sapphire::render::TierTable",
    version: 1,
    data: (
        tiers: [
            (
                // RTX 3070 / RX 6700 XT, M2 Pro: 1440p native, or 4K upsampled by TAA from 1440
                // rows.
                id: DesktopHigh,
                // A discrete GPU, or Apple silicon (an integrated GPU on Metal), with 16 GB:
                // §3.1 budgets 10 GB of RAM. RAM can't tell a GTX 1060 machine apart; a device
                // database will (quality module docs, "Later milestones").
                select_when: [
                    (gpus: [Discrete], min_ram_mib: 14000),
                    (gpus: [Integrated], backends: [Metal], min_ram_mib: 14000),
                ],
                frame_rate: 60,
                gpu_frame_ms: 12.0,
                resolution: (scale: 1.0, max_height: 1440, dynamic_floor: 0.7),
                antialiasing: (msaa: Off, temporal: true),
                bloom_levels: 5,
                light_path: Clustered,
                max_lights: 64,
                shadows: (
                    cascades: 4,
                    resolution: 2048,
                    distance: 120,
                    cached_cascades: 2,
                    character_shadow: true,
                    character_resolution: 1024,
                    filter: Tent5,
                ),
                ambient_occlusion: (capsules: true, gtao: Some((slices: 2, steps: 4, radius: 1.0))),
                volumetric_fog: true,
                screen_space_outlines: true,
                max_particles: 50000,
                lod_bias: 0.0,
                sky: (cube_size: 256, cube_interval: 1, cirrus: true),
                environment: (specular: Full, probes: PerPixel),
                post_effects: (radial_blur_taps: 16),
                foliage: (wind_levels: 3, alpha_to_coverage: true, translucency: true),
                reflections: (cube_size: 128),
            ),
            (
                // GTX 1060 6 GB, Steam Deck, M1 8 GB: 1080p (800p on the Deck), upsampled by
                // TAA on taller displays. Every desktop qualifies, software and paravirtual GPUs
                // included.
                id: DesktopLow,
                frame_rate: 60,
                gpu_frame_ms: 14.0,
                resolution: (scale: 1.0, max_height: 1080, dynamic_floor: 0.7),
                antialiasing: (msaa: Off, temporal: true),
                bloom_levels: 5,
                light_path: Clustered,
                max_lights: 64,
                shadows: (
                    cascades: 4,
                    resolution: 1024,
                    distance: 100,
                    cached_cascades: 2,
                    character_shadow: true,
                    character_resolution: 512,
                    filter: Tent5,
                ),
                ambient_occlusion: (capsules: true, gtao: Some((slices: 2, steps: 4, radius: 1.0))),
                volumetric_fog: true,
                screen_space_outlines: false,
                max_particles: 50000,
                lod_bias: 0.5,
                sky: (cube_size: 256, cube_interval: 1, cirrus: true),
                environment: (specular: Full, probes: PerPixel),
                post_effects: (radial_blur_taps: 12),
                foliage: (wind_levels: 3, alpha_to_coverage: true, translucency: true),
                reflections: (cube_size: 128),
            ),
            (
                // iPhone 15 Pro (A17 Pro), Snapdragon 8 Gen 2+: ~1600×740 → native at 60 fps.
                id: MobileHigh,
                // 8 GB phones, which Android reports a little under 8 GiB; §3.1 budgets 2.8 GB.
                select_when: [
                    (gpus: [Integrated], min_ram_mib: 7000),
                ],
                frame_rate: 60,
                gpu_frame_ms: 13.0,
                resolution: (scale: 1.0, max_height: 740, dynamic_floor: 0.75),
                antialiasing: (msaa: X4, temporal: false),
                bloom_levels: 5,
                light_path: PerObject,
                max_lights: 8,
                shadows: (
                    cascades: 2,
                    resolution: 1024,
                    distance: 50,
                    cached_cascades: 1,
                    character_shadow: false,
                    filter: Tent3,
                ),
                ambient_occlusion: (capsules: true, gtao: Some((slices: 1, steps: 4, radius: 0.75))),
                volumetric_fog: false,
                screen_space_outlines: false,
                max_particles: 8000,
                lod_bias: 0.0,
                sky: (cube_size: 128, cube_interval: 1, cirrus: true),
                environment: (specular: Approximate, probes: PerPixel),
                post_effects: (radial_blur_taps: 8),
                foliage: (wind_levels: 3, alpha_to_coverage: true, translucency: true),
                reflections: (cube_size: 64),
            ),
            (
                // iPhone 12 (A14, 4 GB), Snapdragon 865-class with 6 GB: ~1280×590 → native at
                // 30 fps. The device floor: every phone qualifies.
                id: MobileLow,
                frame_rate: 30,
                gpu_frame_ms: 26.0,
                resolution: (scale: 1.0, max_height: 590, dynamic_floor: 0.75),
                antialiasing: (msaa: X4, temporal: false),
                // Four levels reach 1/16 of the ~590-row scene.
                bloom_levels: 4,
                light_path: PerObject,
                max_lights: 8,
                shadows: (
                    cascades: 2,
                    resolution: 1024,
                    distance: 40,
                    cached_cascades: 1,
                    character_shadow: false,
                    filter: Tent3,
                ),
                ambient_occlusion: (capsules: true, gtao: None),
                volumetric_fog: false,
                screen_space_outlines: false,
                max_particles: 8000,
                lod_bias: 0.5,
                // A face every other frame is a full cube every 0.4 s at 30 fps; the card clouds
                // carry the look without the cirrus layer.
                sky: (cube_size: 64, cube_interval: 2, cirrus: false),
                // The world's highlights go first: a 30 fps phone spends its budget on the
                // characters and the frame's atmosphere.
                environment: (specular: Off, probes: PerVertex),
                post_effects: (radial_blur_taps: 8),
                foliage: (wind_levels: 2, alpha_to_coverage: true, translucency: false),
                reflections: (cube_size: 32),
            ),
        ],
    ),
)
